      "concept": "C0174",
      "prompt": "What is sensor?",
      "answer": "Virtual reality (VR) hardware has three major components: displays (output devices), sensors (input devices), and computers (processing devices).",
      "from_lecture": "13"
     },
     {
      "concept": "C0239",
      "prompt": "What is tracking?",
      "answer": "In the complete view of a virtual reality (VR) system, data flow from the organism to the VR hardware is labeled tracking, data flow from the VR hardware to the organism is labeled stimulation, and bidirectional data flows exist between the VR hardware and the surrounding physical world and between the surrounding physical world and the organism.",
      "from_lecture": "13"
     },
